{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982175-gameline-as-zombie-apocalypse","id":982175,"title":"Gameline As: Zombie Apocalypse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-05T09:41:21-07:00","id":982175,"title":"Gameline As: Zombie Apocalypse","content":"The &quot;Gameline As&quot; bit is probably going to be a repeated pattern. The idea is to look at each listed topic through the lens of each game-line (without copying the thread into every sub-forum).<br /> <br /> Today's topic is: Zombie Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> How would you model a Zombie Apocalypse in each game-line? What impact would it have on people and the supernaturals? What distinct takes could each have?<br /> <br /> I'll start with the rough outline of a few I have. I'll try to add more detail in later.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire - The Revenant Virus</b><br /> Some half-mystical, half-engineered virus has escaped what ever containment it was held in (or was purposefully released) and has now reached pandemic proportions. Anyone infected arises as a feral Revenant some time after death (ranging from a day, to mere moments). The virus isn't immediately fatal (though a Revenant who transmitted it to you by gnawing on your neck might be), so it often spreads undetected, especially by Kindred feeding. The Masquerade is in shambles as hordes of infectious, blood-hungry zombies beseige mortal authorities the world over.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf - Zombie Claimed</b><br /> Some new kind of death-spirit has been sighted in more and more territories. It seems relatively weak and low Rank, but it does not appear to suffer Essence Bleed, instead remaining in Twilight and wandering indefinitely. It also seems to be able to Claim corpses, despite its low Rank, and the corpses don't decay as is usual for an &quot;object&quot; being Claimed. More troubling, it seems to be able to spawn a whole new spirit whenever its Claimed corpse-body kills a person. These things are now &quot;breeding&quot; out of control, and every time some mortal or circumstance &quot;kills&quot; one of the &quot;zombies&quot;, the spirit just wanders off to the nearest corpse or graveyard and Claims again.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy - Nenitu Gone Wild</b><br /> A foolish Sekhem Sorcerer (or perhaps a more foolish Arisen) has unleashed a flawed Utterance and animated a batch of particularly infectious Nenitu who <i>somehow</i> managed to get transported to various population centers and have now spawned an uncontainable swarm of Lifeless killers. Your Cult, and those of your peers, is overtaxed keeping these runaway dead under control in their immediate area, and mortal authorities are taking drastic steps towards anything that even <i>looks</i> like a walking corpse.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist - Who Let The Ghosts Out</b><br /> An Underworld current, warped Ceremony, or just bad karma has caused many, if not all, of the Avernian Gates to open wide and suck specters straight from the depths of the Underworld into the land of the Quick. Many Kerberoi are noticably pissed, but the escapees all seem to have developed the ability to Claim or Possess corpses, and are having a field day. To make matters worse, every time someone gets killed or dies near these escapees, a micro-rift forms and dumps <i>another</i> ghost out, happy to play in the land of the living. Krewes everywhere are overworked, and the news is blaring about &quot;Hell being full&quot; or some other doomsaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-05-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:30:49-07:00","id":982192,"title":"","content":"<b>Promethean: The Sorceror's Apprentice but Corpses</b><br /> An unusually intelligent Pandoran figures out how to make more of itself in an attempt ape the Pilgrimage and become a full-fledged Promethean. One thing leads to another, and now there's a mob of hungry Pandorans trying to feed any way they can. Prometheans are nearly extinct by this point, and humans are next on the menu.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:53:06-07:00","id":982206,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunter: Cheiron Group Done Goofed Up</b><br /> Do I need to say anything else? Way to go, Cheiron. Way to go. Maybe stitching together parts of various dead supernatural stuff in hope for a cheap work force wasn't the best idea after all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:16:39-07:00","id":982219,"title":"","content":"(not really a gameline, but still)-<br /> <br /> <b>Inferno: Hell is Empty</b><br /> Hell is overflowed. Maybe it is the way modern culture works, perhaps it was only a matter of time- but Inferno is full. More of the world is being corrupted than its fire could burn. Smoke rise from the graveyards, souls escape through locked gates and countless dead dug themselves from the ground. Judgement day is coming, the Resurrection has come- yet there are no angels to announce the apocalypse, and no messiah at its end. Only fire and brimstone- and you, surrounded by the living dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:12:08-07:00","id":982296,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage: Children of Regret</b><br /> A Necromancer has lost his loved one, and out of desperation attempted to bring him back to life. His Hubris took over the spell, and the Abyss leaked in. While the dead did returned to life, it wasn't his lover who came back- or perhaps it was, just a bit.. different, and it brought something else with him- something that wanted children of its own. It started to kill, and as it did the thing cut a part of its corrupted Pattern and put it inside of the dead body, and each of the new &quot;children&quot; sought to make more of its kind. Now they are everywhere. Can the local Consilium deal with it before it is too late?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:49:43-07:00","id":982323,"title":"","content":"Hunter: Search for the Source<br /> <br /> Maybe Cheiron did screw up. Maybe TFV got their hands on a real nasty Soviet bio-weapons stockpile. Or the Catholic Church chose poorly on a relic they found. Whatever happened, now hunters across the globe are in a race against time to find patient zero before the last holdouts are overrun, while making sure mankind isn't turned into supernatural chattel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:33:51-07:00","id":982399,"title":"","content":"<b>Werewolf/Geist: Death's Boss is a Jackass</b><br /> Somebody has taken control of a death spirit. This wouldn't normally be an issue, except this is a gorram <i>Dihar</i> that the Fog Men call Kerberos. Death has closed its doors to the dying, and angry ghosts with nowhere else to go have been Claiming corpses. Not to be outdone, starving Death spirits have been doing the same, sometimes even Hive-Claiming with the ghosts. Wolves and Dead Men are far from friends, but in this case, a partnership is looking like a good idea.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage/Genius: Curiosity Killed The Everything</b><br /> When a high-powered Seer started promising his mortal lackeys immortality, things seemed to be going like usual, until one of those clueless loonies decided to debunk it. In public. On live TV. The Paradox blew things sky high at the same time as the resulting Mania Storm of disillusionment hit, and now death has been partly suspended.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: Parliament of Owls</b><br /> They just had to go poking into the smoke-owls, didn't they. Now there's an Owl out there whose bite is infectious, creating wild Draugr without even needing to bother Embracing. They're weak, but the Striges don't care, as long as they get to watch the suffering.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean/Mummy: The Devourer Hungers</b><br /> What do you got when you mix the deathless essence of a Mummy with the raw chaos of the Divine Fire? You get a big ol' mess. It started when a Promethean tried to raise a Mummy's <i>sahu</i> as offspring. The body rose, but not with anything resembling a consciousness. The only thing behind its eyes was fire and the gaping void of Ammut, with the power to make <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviant: Built to Last</b><br /> Some biotech company was working on a genetic therapy that made a person immortal. The downside is that the retroviral &quot;therapy&quot; is infectious, and the first symptom is jacked-up need for nutrition. Guess what has everything a human body needs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T17:27:07-07:00","id":982452,"title":"","content":"<b>Changeling - Garden Variety Zombie</b><br /> The Freehold caught wind too late of some new kind of Hedge-beast plant that is parasitizing bodies, turning them into shambling, nutrient hungry infection vectors. Now the city, and in fact other cities, are infested with ever growing ranks of the floral undead. It <i>really</i> doesn't help that they are draw to Glamour - fear, especially, but the stockpiles in Changelings and Fae-Touched are tempting too.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon - Intruder Alert</b><br /> Some fool Saboteur blew up the wrong Infrastructure at the wrong time and seriously warped the underlying meta-structure Exploits rely upon. Some completely uninvolved Unchained on the other side of the planet tried a simple Raise Dead and got an Intruder. That can create more of itself. Whose copies can create more of <i>themselves</i>, ad nauseam. Even disregarding the widespread panic, and bodily threat, Cover is going to hard to find if humanity goes extinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-06-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:54:17-07:00","id":982492,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast: No Really, It's Like A Movie Out There</b><br /> <br /> Some nutcase of a Namtaru, high on equal parts fear and fundamentalist mania, has come to the conclusion that the entire world needs to be taught a lesson in unity. So, he's torn out a bit of the Primordial Dream representing the primal fear of the outisder that gave rise to zombie movies, injected it in a corpse, and bang, instant plague of the undead that acts exactly as people expect them too, including being numerous enough to ratchet up the tensions on any hapless living they're menacing. Their only weakness? The capacity of people to band together and look cool, which just as expected, makes them little more than gore-filled props. Unfortunately, a lot of Heroes seem to have gotten it in their enormous skulls that this movie is of the self-insert Hard Man Making Hard Decisions genre. Not very conducive to the far easier way of cueing the undead to go back six feet under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-06-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:36:12-07:00","id":982815,"title":"","content":"<b>??? - Send in the Zombie Clowns</b><br /> You know those clowns that keep popping up in the news recently? They were just Patient Zero for a strange new infection that turns its victims into clowns. Zombie Clowns. It would be funny if it wasn't also sad, scary, and life threatening. Bad enough you could get eaten alive - somehow it is worse when the things doing it look like Ronald McDonald.<br /> <br /> [Wanted to use the whole stupid clown scare thing going on, but I have <i>no idea</i> which gameline it would fit under.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:13:48-07:00","id":982956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982175-gameline-as-zombie-apocalypse?p=982815#post982815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>??? - Send in the Zombie Clowns</b><br /> You know those clowns that keep popping up in the news recently? They were just Patient Zero for a strange new infection that turns its victims into clowns. Zombie Clowns. It would be funny if it wasn't also sad, scary, and life threatening. Bad enough you could get eaten alive - somehow it is worse when the things doing it look like Ronald McDonald.<br /> <br /> [Wanted to use the whole stupid clown scare thing going on, but I have <i>no idea</i> which gameline it would fit under.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of virus, prion, or fungus that creates clown-obsessed Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:07:12-07:00","id":996733,"title":"","content":"<b>Leviathan - It's Beginning To Look A Lot Like Fish-men</b><br /> Project Purity was a Marduk Society research project aimed towards developing a retro-virus capable of &quot;inoculating&quot; a person against any Leviathan genes becoming activated, &quot;curing&quot; them of any potential expression of the Wicked Tribe's traits. Except, it was found to be impossible, and the project was cancelled. At least, &quot;officially&quot;. It was moved into an isolated secret research group, run by some of the more black hat members of the society. Since a cure was impossible, the next best thing would be a purge, they reasoned. Once all bearers of the Leviathans' tainted genetics were eliminated, no more throwbacks would be possible from the now pure gene pool. Then the civil war for control of the Marduk Society happened, and in the chaos the experimental virus was released into the atmosphere. It... didn't work as intended. Rather than kill off people descended from the Wicked Tribe, it instead provoked a violent, unstable reaction - almost everyone infected with even a trace of Leviathan genes (which ended up being far more of the population that the group's projections) mutated into a frenzied Hybrid. Nearly mindless, they swarm and attack anyone not like them - a living zombie apocalypse with gills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-01-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}